WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.427 --> 00:00:03.309
Right now, I'm standing on the Palestinian side

2
00:00:03.309 --> 00:00:05.971
of the wall that separates the Palestinians

3
00:00:05.971 --> 00:00:08.280
from the Israelis.

4
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.617
According to the Israeli government,

5
00:00:09.617 --> 00:00:12.098
the separation wall is a security measure

6
00:00:12.098 --> 00:00:14.738
built to protect against terrorist attacks,

7
00:00:14.738 --> 00:00:16.278
and has resulted in a dramatic drop

8
00:00:16.278 --> 00:00:18.907
in Israeli deaths and casualties.

9
00:00:18.907 --> 00:00:20.360
It's also a flash point.

10
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.429
There's been a lot of violence here,

11
00:00:22.429 --> 00:00:25.309
a lot of clashes between the Israeli forces

12
00:00:25.309 --> 00:00:29.476
and Palestinians, rock throwing, tear gas, killings.

13
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.347
And, of course, right here the ultimate symbol

14
00:00:32.347 --> 00:00:33.689
of divisiveness,

15
00:00:33.689 --> 00:00:35.905
(audience laughs)

16
00:00:35.905 --> 00:00:38.505
Donald Trump kissing the guard tower.

17
00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.316
Apparently, he thinks it's his fourth wife.

18
00:00:40.316 --> 00:00:41.894
(audience laughs)

19
00:00:41.894 --> 00:00:43.524
While we were filming at the wall,

20
00:00:43.524 --> 00:00:46.684
I was confronted by a group of pro-Palestinian activists.

21
00:00:46.684 --> 00:00:48.145
What do you think of this wall?

22
00:00:48.145 --> 00:00:49.396
Is this a normal wall?

23
00:00:49.396 --> 00:00:50.229
Well, no.

24
00:00:50.229 --> 00:00:51.802
I don't think any wall like this is normal.

25
00:00:51.802 --> 00:00:52.774
Do you?

26
00:00:52.774 --> 00:00:53.607
I'm Palestinian.

27
00:00:53.607 --> 00:00:55.025
I do not.
Yeah, no.

28
00:00:55.025 --> 00:00:56.705
No, no, no.
Not at all.

29
00:00:56.705 --> 00:00:57.956
It's sad.

30
00:00:57.956 --> 00:00:58.789
It's very sad.

31
00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:00.044
Walls like this.
I've been in prison

32
00:01:00.044 --> 00:01:00.877
at the end of the day.

33
00:01:00.877 --> 00:01:03.516
You don't create peace by segregating people.

34
00:01:03.516 --> 00:01:04.349
And they can't keep saying,

35
00:01:04.349 --> 00:01:05.182
"Oh, well, they throw rocks."

36
00:01:05.182 --> 00:01:06.534
You've got M-16s.

37
00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:07.476
You've got tanks.

38
00:01:07.476 --> 00:01:08.676
You can't compare that.

39
00:01:08.676 --> 00:01:10.094
There's also another side of it

40
00:01:10.094 --> 00:01:12.836
where there are people who would say

41
00:01:12.836 --> 00:01:15.848
we don't want the Jewish State to exist at all.

42
00:01:15.848 --> 00:01:16.681
No, no.
We don't want to accept it

43
00:01:16.681 --> 00:01:17.514
at all.

44
00:01:17.514 --> 00:01:18.655
No, if you speak to Palestinians,

45
00:01:18.655 --> 00:01:19.705
you could go into refugee camps,

46
00:01:19.705 --> 00:01:21.713
which they would never take you, right? Right.

47
00:01:21.713 --> 00:01:22.546
But you would be welcomed.

48
00:01:22.546 --> 00:01:23.429
And people welcome you into their home.

49
00:01:23.429 --> 00:01:24.262
And give you the clothes off their back.

50
00:01:24.262 --> 00:01:25.095
No.

51
00:01:25.095 --> 00:01:25.928
We're on our way to.

52
00:01:25.928 --> 00:01:27.150
We wanted to go to a refugee camp.

53
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:27.983
Which one?

54
00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:28.816
With the IDF.

55
00:01:28.816 --> 00:01:30.599
No, we're not going with the IDF.

56
00:01:30.599 --> 00:01:32.515 line:15%
We were headed.

57
00:01:32.515 --> 00:01:33.348 line:15%
Let me ask you a question.

58
00:01:33.348 --> 00:01:36.502
What do you see as a solution?

59
00:01:36.502 --> 00:01:37.422
As a solution.

60
00:01:37.422 --> 00:01:39.340
Well, one, America has to stop giving Israel

61
00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.302
$10 million a day just for weapons.

62
00:01:41.302 --> 00:01:42.222
Once the weapons stop,

63
00:01:42.222 --> 00:01:43.563
Israel has no choice but to speak,

64
00:01:43.563 --> 00:01:44.913
to talk about peace.

65
00:01:44.913 --> 00:01:47.033
And if American people knew where their money was going,

66
00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:47.993
and the fact that when they,

67
00:01:47.993 --> 00:01:51.014
when, when, when our wonderful orange president

68
00:01:51.014 --> 00:01:53.063
got elected and people are very sad that.

69
00:01:53.063 --> 00:01:56.174
Let's not go after him for having orange hair.

70
00:01:56.174 --> 00:01:57.007
(laughter)

71
00:01:57.007 --> 00:01:57.840
Yeah.

72
00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:58.673
Now you're getting personal.

73
00:01:58.673 --> 00:02:00.563
Now you have a problem with me.

74
00:02:00.563 --> 00:02:01.396
It's his orange face.

75
00:02:01.396 --> 00:02:02.229
It's his face.

76
00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:03.062
No, but it.

77
00:02:03.062 --> 00:02:04.683
That got very personal very fast.

78
00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:05.516
(laughter)

79
00:02:05.516 --> 00:02:06.782
Well, here's what I can tell you.

80
00:02:06.782 --> 00:02:10.294
I can tell you that there's no way my 40-minute program

81
00:02:10.294 --> 00:02:12.513
is gonna satisfy what it is you want me to do.

82
00:02:12.513 --> 00:02:13.883
It's not, it's not that.
Well, hold it.

83
00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:14.716
Let me just finish.

84
00:02:14.716 --> 00:02:16.523
What I do promise to do is make sure

85
00:02:16.523 --> 00:02:18.782
that people who watch this program

86
00:02:18.782 --> 00:02:22.243
will have an idea that this other reality exists.

87
00:02:22.243 --> 00:02:23.153
Thank you for talking to me.

88
00:02:23.153 --> 00:02:23.986
Thank you.

89
00:02:23.986 --> 00:02:24.833
I hope you.
Yeah, and I,

90
00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:26.901
if you're cool with us putting this online.

91
00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:28.494
Yes, we are.
As it unfolded.

92
00:02:28.494 --> 00:02:29.473
I'd be happy to do that.

93
00:02:29.473 --> 00:02:30.306
Okay.

94
00:02:31.662 --> 00:02:34.603 line:15%
The unedited version of this encounter can be found online.

95
00:02:34.603 --> 00:02:35.491 line:15%
But to be fair,

96
00:02:35.491 --> 00:02:38.740 line:15%
I must emphasize we did not have a similar conversation

97
00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:41.323
with the people who dispute these views.

98
00:02:41.323 --> 00:02:42.905
I'm standing here in Aida.

99
00:02:42.905 --> 00:02:46.422
It is one of the oldest Palestinian refugee camps.

100
00:02:46.422 --> 00:02:48.534
And tell us what does this represent?

101
00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:49.367
The opening here.

102
00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.302
This is the gate of 1948.

103
00:02:51.302 --> 00:02:54.193
It symbolize the right of return for the refugees.

104
00:02:54.193 --> 00:02:57.033 line:15%
Our grandfathers, they were forced to leave their

105
00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.545 line:15%
villages, their houses.

106
00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:01.343
So they hold the keys.

107
00:03:01.343 --> 00:03:04.514
After 60 years, we are waiting for the international

108
00:03:04.514 --> 00:03:08.063
community to implement the UN Resolution 194,

109
00:03:08.063 --> 00:03:11.572
that gave us the right to return for our homeland.

110
00:03:11.572 --> 00:03:14.204
UN Resolution 194 came in the aftermath

111
00:03:14.204 --> 00:03:17.074
of Israel's first war with their Arab neighbors.

112
00:03:17.074 --> 00:03:18.783
Whether the refugees fled their homes

113
00:03:18.783 --> 00:03:20.194
or were forced from their homes

114
00:03:20.194 --> 00:03:23.143
is still a hotly disputed question to this day.

115
00:03:23.143 --> 00:03:24.372
The children that live here,

116
00:03:24.372 --> 00:03:27.114
are they growing up in a situation where they have

117
00:03:27.114 --> 00:03:29.674
no expectation that there'll be peace?

118
00:03:29.674 --> 00:03:32.611
We, as Palestinians, we are teaching the people

119
00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:34.674
that we will have peace on this land.

120
00:03:34.674 --> 00:03:36.164
We can live together here.

121
00:03:36.164 --> 00:03:37.354
Would it be possible for me to go in

122
00:03:37.354 --> 00:03:38.754
and talk to some people?

123
00:03:38.754 --> 00:03:39.663
Is that possible?

124
00:03:39.663 --> 00:03:40.772
Yes, we can go.

125
00:03:40.772 --> 00:03:41.605
Hello.

126
00:03:41.605 --> 00:03:42.438
What is your name?

127
00:03:42.438 --> 00:03:43.332
My name is Jedda.

128
00:03:43.332 --> 00:03:44.463
Do you live here in Aida?

129
00:03:44.463 --> 00:03:45.296 line:15%
Mhm.

130
00:03:49.621 --> 00:03:50.454 line:15%
Okay.

131
00:03:51.752 --> 00:03:54.254
Do you feel like people in America understand

132
00:03:54.254 --> 00:03:56.087 line:15%
