133
00:04:11.852 --> 00:04:14.769 line:15%
You couldn't get a visa to come in.

134
00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:19.312 line:15%
What was your masters in?

135
00:04:19.312 --> 00:04:20.704 line:15%
Environmental studies.

136
00:04:20.704 --> 00:04:21.925
Wow.

137
00:04:21.925 --> 00:04:22.758
Very impressive person.

138
00:04:22.758 --> 00:04:23.591
Thank you.

139
00:04:23.591 --> 00:04:24.424
Yeah, best of luck to you.

140
00:04:24.424 --> 00:04:25.257
Thank you.

141
00:04:25.257 --> 00:04:28.133
Did these guys all grow up here in Aida?

142
00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:28.966
Yes.

143
00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:30.744
Who's the cool one here?

144
00:04:30.744 --> 00:04:33.133
Who's the coolest guy here?

145
00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:33.966
Him!

146
00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:35.667
(laughter)

147
00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.167
He's the cool guy.

148
00:04:37.333 --> 00:04:38.166
There's always one.

149
00:04:38.166 --> 00:04:38.999
If you get three kids together,

150
00:04:38.999 --> 00:04:40.053
He's the leader.
there's one cool guy.

151
00:04:40.053 --> 00:04:41.624
You're the boss, right?

152
00:04:41.624 --> 00:04:42.612
Yes.

153
00:04:42.612 --> 00:04:44.116
(laughter)

154
00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:45.078
(audience laughs, claps)

155
00:04:45.078 --> 00:04:45.911
Yes.

156
00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:52.227 line:15%
What do they wanna say to kids their age in America?

157
00:04:53.019 --> 00:04:57.186 line:15%
Would they like to come visit America someday?

158
00:04:57.316 --> 00:05:00.483 line:15%
What would you like to see in America?

159
00:05:01.325 --> 00:05:02.158
Statue of Liberty?

160
00:05:02.158 --> 00:05:02.991
Statue of Liberty?

161
